  "body": "\r\nHi\r\n\r\nI have a setting where most of my Servers are behind an apache reverse proxy in an Internal Network . I followed the instructions to set up synapse server in that network. \r\n\r\nI use this config on my synapse Server\r\n<VirtualHost *:80>\r\n    ProxyPass /_matrix http://127.0.0.1:8008/_matrix nocanon\r\n    ProxyPassReverse /_matrix http://127.0.0.1:8008/_matrix\r\n</VirtualHost>\r\n\r\n<VirtualHost *:8448>\r\n    ProxyPass /_matrix http://127.0.0.1:8008/_matrix nocanon\r\n    ProxyPassReverse /_matrix http://127.0.0.1:8008/_matrix\r\n</VirtualHost>\r\n\r\n\r\nI use this apache config on my reverse proxy\r\nAlias _matrix /_matrix\r\n\r\n\tProxyPass /_matrix http://192.168.13.85/_matrix nocanon\r\n\tProxyPassReverse /_matrix http://192.168.13.85/_matrix \r\n\r\n\r\nApache brings me a 404 Page\r\n\r\nNo Such Resource\r\n\r\nSorry. No luck finding that resource.\r\n\r\n\r\nI there a way to set up synapse in such an environment ? \r\nDoes anybody have tips for me ? \r\n\r\n",
